issue_context.body:
When getting or setting a field using reflection, `System.ArgumentException` is thrown.

See also Mono issue at https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/issues/97830.

Repro:
```
FieldInfo fi = typeof(MyStructWithFunctionPointers).GetField(nameof(MyStructWithFunctionPointers.s_fcnPtr))!;
object value = fi.GetValue(null)!;
Console.WriteLine(value.GetType());
Console.WriteLine(value);

public struct MyStructWithFunctionPointers
{
    public unsafe static delegate*<void> s_fcnPtr = (delegate*<void>)45;
    public unsafe delegate*<void> fcnPtr = (delegate*<void>)44;

    public MyStructWithFunctionPointers() { }
}
```

Output:
```
Unhandled Exception: System.ArgumentException: Type must be a Pointer. (Parameter 'ptr')
   at System.Reflection.Pointer.Box(Void*, Type) + 0x9a
   at ConsoleApp214.Program.Main(String[] args) + 0x41
   at ConsoleApp214!<BaseAddress>+0xe3700
```

Expected (same as CoreClr):
```
System.IntPtr
45
```
